{{!--
  Classic-Ember `.hbs` consumer using <ClassicCard> with NO JS import.
  Mirrors ember-website's `<EsCard>` pattern: PascalCase tag resolved
  at runtime via Ember's container resolver, looking up
  `classic-card-addon/components/classic-card`.

  At runtime the component renders `<li class="classic-card"
  ...attributes>{{yield}}</li>`. So inside `<ul>`, the resulting DOM is
  valid (`<li>` directly under `<ul>`).

  Without the by-name lookup, our plugin transparent-blanks
  <ClassicCard>, the inner content (potentially structural like
  another `<ul>` or `<div>`) floats directly into the outer `<ul>`,
  and `element-permitted-content` FP-fires.
--}}
<ul>
  <ClassicCard>
    <ul>
      <li>nested item</li>
    </ul>
  </ClassicCard>
</ul>
